                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "aacfe43c-d02b-3a5e-97cb-e5e3c1c055c4",
                        "entry_id": "5e69819f-b3ce-34a8-b6e7-1a8148570287",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A cloth stretched over another space, such as that stretched below the roof of the Royal Albert Hall."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "85f3e906-6958-45e0-98a8-920adddf64fb",
                                "sense_id": "aacfe43c-d02b-3a5e-97cb-e5e3c1c055c4",
                                "text": "In accordance with the epochal significance of the occasion, Berlin was decked out as never before in its history. […] A velarium suspended over Unter den Linden depicted the great military victories that had finally brought Germany its unity."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "060660cf-8dff-404f-852d-9212ae84394e",
                                "sense_id": "aacfe43c-d02b-3a5e-97cb-e5e3c1c055c4",
                                "text": "Royal Albert Hall [was dedicated] by the Prince of Wales (later King Edward VII). As The Times reported on the next day: 'The address [...] was somewhat marred by an echo [...]'. To Col. Scott, the designer of the huge roof structure, this acoustic problem was a mere irritant which could be solved by a velarium of cloth (weighing 1+¹⁄₄ tons) stretched underneath the roof. But in spite of experiments with the height of the velarium, the echo persisted […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
